.SH "نام (NAME)"
lr_processmail \- read an email message and invoke lr_log2mail(1)
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBlr_processmail\fR \fIservice\fR
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBlr_processmail\fR reads an email message from STDIN, parses the message
using \fBlr_getbody\fR\|(1) and invokes \fBlr_log2mail\fR\|(1) to process the extracted 
log file.
.PP
The environment variable LR_ID is used as an identifier, which shows up
in debug messages, and in names of temporary files, so that Lire jobs
can get tracked.  A Lire job currently is identified with one email
message or log file.
.PP
This script is invoked by \fBlr_spool\fR\|(1).
.PP
The files specified in the \fIlr_mail_signature\fR and
\&\fIlr_mail_disclaimer\fR configurartion variables are sent along the
generated report.
.PP
If an error occurs in the report generation process, an email message
explaining possible sources for the error will be sent to the email
addresses.
.PP
The \fB\-o xml\fR format is useful in the case the log file was anonymized
so that it can be deanonymized before being formatted using
\&\fBlr_xml2report\fR\|(1) or \fBlr_xml2mail\fR\|(1). When using that format, the file
specified in the \fIlr_mail_explanation\fR configuration variable will be
included in the outgoing message.
.SH "مثال (EXAMPLE)"
.IX Header "EXAMPLE"
.Vb 1
\& $ lr_processmail combined < /var/spool/lire/done/985327208.21242.mailhost
.Ve
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBlr_spool\fR\|(1), documentation in the Lire User Manual
